## Shipping, warranty, and returns

Shipping: Scrubo ships floor scrubbers and sweepers across Canada, 99% assembled (reattach the squeegee; unfold the handle on some models; reconnect the batteries). Shipping is $80 per machine. Remote or rural deliveries may require a business address, terminal pickup (Manitoulin or Day & Ross), and possibly an extra shipping fee. Carriers are Ace Courier, Day & Ross or Manitoulin Transport, typically LTL ground. Free pickup is available at the Port Coquitlam headquarters; pickup units are fully assembled. Every machine receives a pre-delivery inspection. Preparation typically takes 1–2 business days. Typical transit times after preparation, in business days: British Columbia 2–4; Alberta 3–4; Ontario 5; Quebec 5–7; Northern territories approximately 7–14. The site also states that Scrubo ships throughout the United States; US rates and times are not published.

Warranty: 6-month limited warranty, starting when the original owner receives the machine, on electrical components (including battery, charger, vacuum and brush motors, controller, LCD panel, key lock assembly and other electrical parts). Parts only; labour is not covered. The customer pays shipping of a covered component to Scrubo and of the replacement back, unless Scrubo agrees in writing to pay shipping. Report issues by website, email or phone; the team aims to respond within 24 hours, with customer service agents available 6 days a week. Scrubo says it identifies about 99% of issues remotely and can ship parts to the address on file. Mechanics can assist by phone; video tutorials are on YouTube. Service and repairs are available at the Port Coquitlam facility. Scrubo also says it has partnerships with repair shops and mechanics throughout Canada (the store-locator page does not currently list them).

Returns: returns are allowed within 7 days. Unopened, new and unused machines: 15% restocking fee. Opened and used for more than 1 hour: 25% restocking fee. The customer arranges return freight, or a Scrubo return label is deducted from the refund. The site states that the average cost to ship one pallet across Canada is $250. The machine must be returned in its original packing. Orders can be cancelled free of charge until they have shipped; once a valid tracking number exists, the return policy applies.

Payment options that are published: pay on scrubo.ca; Shop Pay / Affirm financing at checkout (minimum order $1000; APR 0–31.99% where available, subject to eligibility and provincial limits); business leasing through Grenke (GL Leasing British Columbia Inc.) for Canadian businesses (and US businesses only through a Canadian entity), $750–$100,000, no down payment, one-time $115 setup fee, $10 + tax buyout at end of term, subject to credit approval. Qualified businesses and municipalities can set up Net 30 terms by contacting Scrubo; Scrubo will send a short application. Purchase orders can be accepted under the same arrangement. Contact Scrubo for multi-unit quotes.

